  <running_head>INSTITUTIONUM</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">§. 1. De quibus omnibus non licet</l>
    <l n="2">ex profcfo agere, fed tantum paucissi-</l>
    <l n="3">ma annotare. Expansio &amp; contractio</l>
    <l n="4">inperfectissimæ animalium speciei con-</l>
    <l n="5">venit, quæ ideo Zoophytis accensen-</l>
    <l n="6">tur, qualia sunt, quæ uno in loco subs-</l>
    <l n="7">istunt, &amp; aliqua parte aliam propel-</l>
    <l n="8">lunt, aliqua attrahunt. Quanquam</l>
    <l n="9">aliquando sola remissio actionis unam</l>
    <l n="10">actionem supplere possit. Quæ reptatu</l>
    <l n="11">locomoventur pariter attractione &amp;</l>
    <l n="12">pulsu utuntur. Nam terræ affirmata</l>
    <l n="13">pofticam partem attrahunt, verum an-</l>
    <l n="14">teriorem extendunt. Natatus a pisci-</l>
    <l n="15">bus pinnis peragitur, quatenus firmatæ</l>
    <l n="16">sunt in aqua corpus partim attrahunt,</l>
    <l n="17">partim propellunt: At ab aliis natanti-</l>
    <l n="18">bus peragitur per partes impellentes</l>
    <l n="19">maxime. Volatus peragitur, quatenus</l>
    <l n="20">volantia aerem subjectum quietum aliis</l>
    <l n="21">comprehendentia corpus elevant, &amp;</l>
    <l n="22">varie impelluut. Gressus vero per pedes</l>
    <l n="23">celebratur, quatenus illi terræ instantes</l>
    <l n="24">&amp; per vices moti corpus transferunt.</l>
    <l n="25">Saltus etiam terram aut aliud sirmum</l>
    <l n="26">suppositum requirit &amp; impulsu corpus</l>
    <l n="27">de loco in locum transfert.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">§. 2. Atque particularius de his agit</l>
    <l n="29">Philosophus I. de incessu animal. &amp;</l>
    <l n="30">Hieron. Fabric. ab Aquapend. tr. de</l>
    <l n="31">motu</l>
  </main_text>
